The legal text at the URL above is the licence. The summary below is a
convenience, not a substitute for it, and the legal text wins on any conflict.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT YOU MAY DO
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  * Include Candy in a modpack and distribute that modpack, on Modrinth,
    CurseForge, a launcher, a server pack or your own site. You do not need to
    ask first.
  * Redistribute the jar unmodified.
  * Modify Candy and share your modified version.
  * Record, stream and monetise gameplay footage. Video monetisation is not
    what "NonCommercial" restricts here — playing the mod on camera and earning
    ad or sponsor revenue from that video is fine, with no permission needed.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CONDITIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  * Attribution (BY) — credit "Candy by PhotonPulse" and link back to
    https://github.com/omer-faruk-g/Candy. In a modpack, a line in the
    mod list or credits is enough.
  * NonCommercial (NC) — do not sell Candy itself, do not put it behind a
    paywall, and do not make it a paid perk. A pack that includes Candy must
    not be sold.
  * ShareAlike (SA) — if you distribute a modified Candy, it carries this same
    licence.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NOT COVERED BY THIS LICENCE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  * The name "Candy" as a mod identity, and the project's branding. You may say
    your pack contains Candy; do not publish a renamed or rebranded fork as if
    it were the original.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
LICENCE HISTORY — READ THIS IF YOU ALREADY HAVE A COPY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Earlier commits of this repository carried the GNU Affero General Public
License v3 text, while the mod metadata declared "ARR". That was a mistake on
our side, not a trap: the two contradicted each other and gave no clear answer
to "may I put this in a pack?".

If you received a copy of Candy under the AGPL-3.0 text (anything up to and
including release v8.4.0), that grant stands for that copy. We are not trying
to retract it and could not. CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 applies from the next release
onwards.

